  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Livestock-Food Systems Development (LFSD) Component -Kassala project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project targets two states, Kassala and Gedref states, in eastern Sudan; the project will conducted in 9 localities. Kassala state hosts one of the largest livestock populations, estimated to be 14.4 livestock heads, about 15.0 % of the total Sudanese livestock population. The state also supports a similar number of additional livestock, which passes through seasonally. The main domestic livestock is cattle, sheep, goats, and camels.</narrative>
  </description>
